{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-032-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/RouteHarvestCaptureTests.cs","line":73,"method":"DestroyedConverter_InactiveScan_ClosesWindow","category":"T2","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RouteHarvestCapture.cs:51; drop the close branch -> both red","what_it_asserts":"EvaluateTransition(anyActive=false, windowOpen=true) returns Close.","why_weak":"Byte-identical behavior to the EvaluateTransition_Matrix theory cell InlineData(false, true, Close); the destroyed-converter framing is comment-only, no new input or seam.","proposed_action":"Delete the Fact and move its comment onto the matching theory row, or extend it to drive the recorder Unity-null cache scan so it actually pins the inactive classification.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-032-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/RouteHarvestCaptureTests.cs","line":210,"method":"OpenWindow_PopulatesSpanLocationAndFlags","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RouteHarvestCapture.cs:141; drop the harvest- WindowId prefix -> red","what_it_asserts":"OpenWindow stamps StartUT, IsOpen, NaN EndUT, the two recording-boundary flags, the start manifest, BodyName, SituationAtOpen, converter count and the WindowId prefix.","why_weak":"The name claims location coverage but Latitude/Longitude/Altitude (RouteHarvestCapture.cs:147-149) are never asserted; swapping the latitude and longitude assignments, which feed the M2 Phase 5 harvest-origin endpoint, leaves the test green.","proposed_action":"Assert window.Latitude == -0.55, window.Longitude == 78.25 and window.Altitude == 2412.5 from the OpenTestWindow fixture values.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-032-03","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/RouteHarvestCaptureTests.cs","line":116,"method":"RailsExitFunnel_SurvivesSteadyStatePollsUntilTheClose","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RouteHarvestCapture.cs:83; return true for None -> red","what_it_asserts":"A run of None polls leaves railsExitPending armed, and the eventual Close consumes it and is labelled rails-exit.","why_weak":"The trigger label at lines 142-144 is computed by the test itself from a local bool, so that assertion is a tautology; the remaining content duplicates the ShouldConsumeRailsExitFunnel theory.","proposed_action":"Drop the inline trigger-label block, or route the label through the production labelling site (IsRailsExitLabelStillValid plus the recorder trigger selection) so the string assertion pins a production line.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-logistics-route-032-04","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/RouteLiveAnchorTests.cs","line":217,"method":"LiveBindSet_ClearsWhenFrameAdvances","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RelativeAnchorResolver.cs:299; remove the per-frame Clear() -> red","what_it_asserts":"After a bind at frame 30 and a second bind at frame 31, only the frame-31 id reads as live-bound.","why_weak":"The inline comment states the frame-30 id is exactly one frame back and still within tolerance while the assertion requires it to be false; a reader repairing the test against its comment would invert a correct assertion.","proposed_action":"Fix the comment to state that RecordLiveBoundAnchor clears the set on a frame change, so the one-frame tolerance only applies when no later bind occurred.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"coverage","sut":"RouteHarvestCapture","sut_file":"Source/Parsek/RouteHarvestCapture.cs","sut_line":160,"case_kind":"negative","proposed_name":"RouteHarvestCapture_NullWindow_CloseReopenAndManifestAreQuietNoOps","sketch":"Call CloseWindow(null, 2000.0, manifest, true), ReopenWindow(null) and ComputeWindowHarvestedManifest(null); assert no throw and that the manifest call returns an empty, non-null dictionary.","guards":"The three null guards (RouteHarvestCapture.cs:160, 176, 200) are the only thing between a recorder poll racing a window teardown and a NullReferenceException thrown out of the physics-frame path; none is currently exercised.","risk":"recording"}
